OL,3,GNEWSAHistoric garden adapts as hosepipe
OL,4,Aban takes effect
OL,5,
OL,6,FGardeners at a historic property say
OL,7,Fthey are using less water in the
OL,8,Fgrounds as they adapt to hotter, drier
OL,9,Fconditions.
OL,11,FAt the National Trust's Kingston Lacy
OL,12,Fin Dorset, staff have reduced watering
OL,13,Fand introduced drought-tolerant
OL,14,Fplanting ahead of the Wessex Water hose
OL,15,Fpipe ban, which came into force on
OL,16,FTuesday.
OL,18,FThe changes are part of a long-term
OL,19,Feffort to cut water use and respond to
OL,20,Fclimate change, with some trees already
OL,21,Fshowing signs of stress.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,334,330,200,160,0,100
